<Layout
  title="Instinct - Hardware - Rycode"
  description="The custom Instinct GPU is based on the MI450 architecture, with Venice EPYC CPUs, ROCm, and Helios. MI300 and MI350 are the series Meta already runs."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Chips</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Instinct</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">AMD Instinct. The named new chip is a custom GPU based on the MI450 architecture. MI300 and MI350 are series Meta already runs. The purchase is on the <a href="/ai/hardware/chips/meta/">Meta stack</a>.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">MI450</h2>
    <p>On 24 February 2026 AMD said the first deployment uses a custom Instinct GPU based on the MI450 architecture, for Meta's workloads at gigawatt scale. It is paired with 6th Gen AMD EPYC CPUs codenamed Venice, ROCm, and the AMD Helios rack-scale architecture. Shipments for the first gigawatt begin in the second half of 2026. The purchase is up to 6 gigawatts of Instinct GPUs.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">MI300 and MI350</h2>
    <p>The same 24 February 2026 release says Meta already runs millions of AMD EPYC CPUs and significant deployments of Instinct MI300 and MI350 series GPUs.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://ir.amd.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/1279/amd-and-meta-announce-expanded-strategic-partnership-to-deploy-6-gigawatts-of-amd-gpus">AMD, 24 February 2026</a></li>
      <li><a href="/ai/hardware/chips/meta/">Meta stack</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
